    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it felt much bigger than just \"mood contagion\" though. like, looking back, that guy was a key player in that specific sector of the market, and his sudden shift in composure probably prevented a chain reaction of bad decisions in his office today. i'm starting to realize these aren't just random coincidences. if i can start mapping out these patterns, i might be able to calculate how much \"weight\" a single interaction carries. how would i go about calculating the systemic impact of a single stabilized variable like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
